# ArcToon Post-Processing Framework Redesign

> Date: 2026-04-12 | Status: Design Phase
> Reference: ScriptablePostProcessor

---

## 1. Goals

Completely rewrite the post-processing framework as new code. Old framework stays untouched until new one is verified.

- **Composable config**: PostProcessConfig holds a List of settings, freely add/remove effects
- **Unified interface**: Every processor is `Render(cmd, source, destination)`, no exceptions
- **Self-contained resources**: Each processor owns its internal RTHandles (e.g. Bloom pyramid)
- **Ping-Pong dispatch**: PostProcessPass owns TempRTA/B, processors never see the chain
- **One class = one effect**: Adding a new effect = one file

---

## 2. Reference Framework Key Insight: Ping-Pong

```
CameraColor ──blit──→ TempA
    Processor[0].Render(TempA → TempB)  →  Swap(A,B)
    Processor[1].Render(TempA → TempB)  →  Swap(A,B)
    ...
    Processor[N].Render(TempA → TempB)  →  Swap(A,B)
TempA ──blit──→ postFXResult
```

Every processor sees only `(source, destination)`. Bloom internally uses 20+ intermediate RTs, but externally it is still just `source → destination`. The ping-pong buffer management is the dispatcher's job, not the processor's.

---

## 3. Architecture

### 3.1 Config Layer

```
PostProcessConfig (ScriptableObject)
└── List<PostProcessSettings> settings   ← freely add/remove in Inspector
    ├── [0] BloomSettings (Order=100)
    ├── [1] ColorGradingSettings (Order=200)
    └── [2] FXAASettings (Order=900)
```

**PostProcessSettings** — abstract base, serializable:
```csharp
[Serializable]
public abstract class PostProcessSettings
{
    public abstract int Order { get; }
    public bool enabled = true;
}
```

**PostProcessConfig** — ScriptableObject container:
```csharp
[CreateAssetMenu(menuName = "Rendering/ArcToon Post Process Config")]
public class PostProcessConfig : ScriptableObject
{
    [SerializeReference]
    public List<PostProcessSettings> settings = new();

    public T GetSettings<T>() where T : PostProcessSettings
        => settings.OfType<T>().FirstOrDefault();

    public bool HasSettings<T>() where T : PostProcessSettings
        => settings.OfType<T>().Any();
}
```

Key: uses `[SerializeReference]` so Unity can serialize polymorphic list items in Inspector.

Each concrete settings class (BloomSettings, ColorGradingSettings, FXAASettings, etc.) contains only the parameters for that effect. No more god-object PostFXConfig.

### 3.2 Processor Layer

**PostProcessor** — abstract base:
```csharp
public abstract class PostProcessor : IDisposable
{
    public abstract string Name { get; }
    public abstract int Order { get; }

    /// Check if this processor should run this frame.
    public abstract bool IsActive(PostProcessConfig config, CameraRenderer renderer);

    /// Per-frame setup (allocate/resize internal RTs, cache settings, etc.)
    public virtual void Setup(PostProcessConfig config, CameraRenderer renderer) { }

    /// Core render: read from source, write to destination.
    /// Internal complexity (Bloom pyramid, LUT bake, etc.) is fully encapsulated.
    public abstract void Render(CommandBuffer cmd, RTHandle source, RTHandle destination);

    public virtual void Dispose() { }
}
```

**Critical design point**: `Render(cmd, source, destination)` — no RenderResources, no PostFXResources, no public intermediate RT. Everything the processor needs internally, it owns privately.

### 3.3 Dispatch Layer (PostProcessPass)

```csharp
public class PostProcessPass : RenderPassBase
{
    public override string Name => "Post Process";

    private readonly List<PostProcessor> processors = new();
    private readonly List<PostProcessor> activeProcessors = new();

    private RTHandle tempRTA;
    private RTHandle tempRTB;

    public PostProcessPass()
    {
        // Register built-in processors
        processors.Add(new BloomProcessor());
        processors.Add(new ColorGradingProcessor());
        processors.Add(new FXAAProcessor());
        processors.Sort((a, b) => a.Order.CompareTo(b.Order));
    }

    public override void Execute(CommandBuffer cmd, ScriptableRenderContext context)
    {
        var config = renderer.PostProcessConfig;  // new config type
        if (config == null || !config.AreApplicableTo(Camera))
        {
            resources.PostFX.postFXResult = resources.Camera.colorAttachment;
            return;
        }

        // Collect active processors
        activeProcessors.Clear();
        foreach (var p in processors)
        {
            if (p.IsActive(config, renderer))
            {
                p.Setup(config, renderer);
                activeProcessors.Add(p);
            }
        }

        if (activeProcessors.Count == 0)
        {
            resources.PostFX.postFXResult = resources.Camera.colorAttachment;
            return;
        }

        // Allocate ping-pong buffers
        var desc = GetPostFXDescriptor(renderer);
        RenderingUtils.ReAllocateIfNeeded(ref tempRTA, desc, name: "_PostFX_TempA");

        if (activeProcessors.Count == 1)
        {
            // Single effect: source → TempA, then TempA becomes result
            activeProcessors[0].Render(cmd, resources.Camera.colorAttachment, tempRTA);
        }
        else
        {
            // Multiple effects: blit source → TempA, then ping-pong
            RenderingUtils.ReAllocateIfNeeded(ref tempRTB, desc, name: "_PostFX_TempB");
            Blit(cmd, resources.Camera.colorAttachment, tempRTA);

            foreach (var p in activeProcessors)
            {
                p.Render(cmd, tempRTA, tempRTB);
                (tempRTA, tempRTB) = (tempRTB, tempRTA); // swap
            }
        }

        // TempA now holds the final result
        resources.PostFX.postFXResult = tempRTA;
    }

    public void Dispose()
    {
        tempRTA?.Release();
        tempRTB?.Release();
        foreach (var p in processors) p.Dispose();
    }
}
```

### 3.4 Concrete Processors

#### BloomProcessor

```csharp
public class BloomProcessor : PostProcessor
{
    public override string Name => "Bloom";
    public override int Order => 100;

    // ---- Internal resources (self-owned, not in any public container) ----
    private RTHandle prefilter;
    private RTHandle[] pyramid = new RTHandle[2 * MaxPyramidLevels];
    private const int MaxPyramidLevels = 16;
    private Material material;
    private int stepCount;
    private BloomSettings settings;

    public override bool IsActive(PostProcessConfig config, CameraRenderer renderer)
    {
        var s = config.GetSettings<BloomSettings>();
        if (s == null || !s.enabled) return false;
        // ... size/iteration checks ...
        return true;
    }

    public override void Setup(PostProcessConfig config, CameraRenderer renderer)
    {
        settings = config.GetSettings<BloomSettings>();
        material ??= ShaderResourceManager.AcquireTransientMaterial("Hidden/ArcToon/Bloom");
        // Allocate/resize internal pyramid RTs ...
    }

    public override void Render(CommandBuffer cmd, RTHandle source, RTHandle destination)
    {
        // 1. Prefilter: source → prefilter
        // 2. Downsample pyramid: prefilter → pyramid[0] → pyramid[1] → ...
        // 3. Upsample pyramid: ... → pyramid[1] → pyramid[0]
        // 4. Final combine: pyramid[0] + source → destination
        //
        // All intermediate RTs are private fields of this class.
        // 'source' is read-only input, 'destination' is the only output.
    }

    public override void Dispose()
    {
        prefilter?.Release();
        foreach (var rt in pyramid) rt?.Release();
    }
}
```

#### ColorGradingProcessor

```csharp
