#### FXAAProcessor

```csharp
public class FXAAProcessor : PostProcessor
{
    public override string Name => "FXAA";
    public override int Order => 900;

    private Material material;

    public override bool IsActive(PostProcessConfig config, CameraRenderer renderer)
    {
        var s = config.GetSettings<FXAASettings>();
        return s != null && s.enabled && renderer.CameraAdditiveData.allowFXAA;
    }

    public override void Render(CommandBuffer cmd, RTHandle source, RTHandle destination)
    {
        // Configure keywords + draw: source → destination
    }
}
```

#### Adding a new effect (e.g. RadialBlur)

```csharp
// One file, that's it.
[Serializable]
public class RadialBlurSettings : PostProcessSettings
{
    public override int Order => 150;
    public float blurRadius;
    public Vector2 center = new(0.5f, 0.5f);
}

public class RadialBlurProcessor : PostProcessor
{
    public override string Name => "Radial Blur";
    public override int Order => 150;
    private Material material;

    public override bool IsActive(PostProcessConfig config, CameraRenderer renderer)
    {
        var s = config.GetSettings<RadialBlurSettings>();
        return s != null && s.enabled && s.blurRadius > 0f;
    }

    public override void Render(CommandBuffer cmd, RTHandle source, RTHandle destination)
    {
        cmd.SetGlobalVector("_RadialBlurParams", ...);
        FullScreenDraw(cmd, source, destination, material, 0);
    }
}
```

Then register in PostProcessPass constructor: `processors.Add(new RadialBlurProcessor());`

---

## 4. Data Flow Comparison

### Old Framework
```
PostFXConfig (god object, all settings)
    → PostFXPass (hardcoded chain)
        → BloomPass.Execute(cmd, resources, renderer, config, stack)
            writes to resources.PostFX.bloomResult  ← public shared RT
        → ColorGradingPass.Execute(cmd, resources, renderer, config, stack, source)
            writes to resources.PostFX.colorGradingResult  ← public shared RT
        → AntiAliasingPass.Execute(cmd, resources, renderer, stack, source)
            writes to resources.PostFX.fxaaResult  ← public shared RT
    → resources.PostFX.postFXResult = last result
```

### New Framework
```
PostProcessConfig (composable list of settings)
    → PostProcessPass (generic ping-pong dispatcher)
        → Blit(colorAttachment → TempA)
        → BloomProcessor.Render(TempA → TempB)     Swap
            internal: prefilter, pyramid[] (private)
        → ColorGradingProcessor.Render(TempA → TempB)  Swap
            internal: colorLUT (private)
        → FXAAProcessor.Render(TempA → TempB)      Swap
    → postFXResult = TempA
```

---

## 5. Migration from Old PostFXResources

Old `PostFXResources` held all intermediate RTs publicly. After migration:

| Old (PostFXResources) | New (owned by) |
|---|---|
| bloomPrefilter, bloomPyramid[], bloomResult | BloomProcessor (private) |
| colorLUT, colorGradingResult | ColorGradingProcessor (private) |
| fxaaResult | eliminated (uses TempRT) |
| postFXResult | PostProcessPass.tempRTA (after final swap) |

`PostFXResources` can be reduced to only hold `postFXResult` (the alias read by CopyFinalPass), or eliminated entirely if CopyFinalPass reads from PostProcessPass directly.

---

## 6. Shader Strategy

Old framework: single uber-shader `Hidden/ArcToon/Post FX Stack` with pass index enum.

New framework: **each processor can use its own shader**. This is optional — existing effects can continue sharing a single shader if desired, but new effects are free to use independent shaders.

The old `PostFXStack` class (with its `Pass` enum and bound Material) is replaced by a static utility:

```csharp
public static class PostFXUtility
{
    private static readonly int sourceTextureID = Shader.PropertyToID("_PostFXSource");

    public static void FullScreenDraw(CommandBuffer cmd,
        RenderTargetIdentifier src, RenderTargetIdentifier dst,
        Material material, int pass)
    {
        cmd.SetGlobalTexture(sourceTextureID, src);
        cmd.SetRenderTarget(dst, RenderBufferLoadAction.DontCare, RenderBufferStoreAction.Store);
        cmd.DrawProcedural(Matrix4x4.identity, material, pass, MeshTopology.Triangles, 3);
    }

    public static void Blit(CommandBuffer cmd,
        RenderTargetIdentifier src, RenderTargetIdentifier dst)
    {
        FullScreenDraw(cmd, src, dst, /* copy material */, 0);
    }
}
```

---

## 7. Implementation Plan

### Phase 1: Infrastructure
1. Create `PostProcessSettings` base class
2. Create `PostProcessConfig` ScriptableObject with `[SerializeReference]` list
3. Create `PostProcessor` base class
4. Create `PostFXUtility` static helper
5. Create `PostProcessPass` with ping-pong dispatch

### Phase 2: Migrate Effects
6. Create `BloomSettings` + `BloomProcessor` (port existing Bloom logic)
7. Create `ColorGradingSettings` + `ColorGradingProcessor` (port existing ColorGrading logic)
8. Create `FXAASettings` + `FXAAProcessor` (port existing FXAA logic)

### Phase 3: Integration
9. Wire `PostProcessPass` into `CameraRenderer` (replace old `PostFXPass`)
10. Create new `PostProcessConfig` asset, migrate old `PostFXConfig` parameter values
11. Remove old framework code

### Phase 4: Verification
12. Per-effect visual comparison (screenshot diff)
13. Edge cases: no effects active, single effect, all effects, Scene View

### Verification Checklist (per processor)
- [ ] `IsActive()` conditions match old behavior
- [ ] All `SetGlobalTexture/Float/Vector/Color` calls preserved
- [ ] All `SetKeyword` calls preserved
- [ ] Draw call sequence identical
- [ ] Output visually identical to old framework

